  "note": "Base attributes and the bonus pool per class, plus the skill-choice walk the creation flow consumes. The walk is five records per class, in class order: a record of type 1 rolls the skill after it from that skill's governing attribute, and a count record offers that many picks. Every class rolls attack and defense first, because a class that never rolls attack begins at zero, where the to-hit roll cannot reach a success and no blow ever lands. The skill numbers are the donor's player-data order (src/player/playerdatskills.cs: byte 0x22 + skillNo). Values are Ours (small, readable); the original's SKILLS.DAT class rows are importer work that has not landed, and this pack claims no fidelity.",
